// The Verdance, read off its walls (NAR-15, docs/story/environment.md). The thing speaks, never a person;
// reading changes nothing. The catalog is `Dressing`. The gate's inscription is `Gate_Inscription`.

title: Road_Milestone
---
Milestone: HALDEN, ONE DAY'S FLIGHT. The letters are cut for eyes a long way up. #still #line:0137859
Milestone: Chalked beside it, at a walker's height: "Nine on foot. Bring bread." #plant:5.6 #still #line:0429281
===

title: Cloister_Tapestry
---
Tapestry: Undyed wool. The Verdance woven in, and every village a knot. #still #line:087a530
Tapestry: Some knots have been unpicked, gently. Their threads hang loose. None is cut. #still #line:0b7ed4e
<<if place_fate("Verdance_Aldermere_2") == "released">>
    Tapestry: Aldermere's knot is open now. Its thread hangs with the others. #still #line:09f9dc6
<<endif>>
===

title: Library_Lectern
---
Lectern: A reading list, pinned where the monks would see it. One title on it. #still #line:02ef41e
Lectern: The pin has rusted into the wood. The list has not yellowed. #plant:5.1 #still #line:0ac3908
===
